---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How to Fish Game Help explains its analytics, hosting, advertising, and visitor-data practices." canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <article class="narrow section prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Effective August 26, 2026</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This site serves static informational guides. Google Analytics is <strong>{site.analyticsEnabled ? 'enabled' : 'disabled'}</strong> in this build, Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled on the production domain, Adsterra advertising units are currently disabled, and Google AdSense advertisements are not enabled.</p>

    <h2>Google Analytics and consent</h2>
    {site.analyticsEnabled ? (
      <>
        <p>This site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand general site usage and improve its guides.</p>
        <p>Google Analytics operates with Google Consent Mode. Before the Google tag loads, analytics storage, advertising storage, advertising user data, and ad personalization are set to denied. The current site does not provide an on-site control that grants or updates those consent states, so they remain denied.</p>
        <p>In this state, Google Analytics does not read or write Analytics cookies, but may send limited cookieless measurement signals to Google. These signals may include technical and contextual information such as the requested page, event type, timestamp, browser or device information, screen resolution, referrer, consent state, and information transmitted as part of ordinary internet communication.</p>
        <p>The site tag disables Google Signals and ad-personalization signals. Its initial page-view configuration sends the site origin and path without search parameters. We do not intentionally send names, email addresses, phone numbers, account identifiers, form contents, purchase details, or other directly identifying information to Google Analytics.</p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <p>Google Analytics is disabled in this build, so this build sends no GA4 measurement request.</p>
        <p>Google Analytics operates with Google Consent Mode when enabled. Analytics storage, advertising storage, advertising user data, and ad personalization default to denied before the tag loads. In that state, Google Analytics does not read or write Analytics cookies, but may send limited cookieless measurement signals to Google.</p>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>Google AdSense and advertising cookies</h2>
    <p>This site may use Google AdSense to display third-party advertisements. When advertising is enabled, third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies, local storage, web beacons, IP addresses, and similar identifiers to deliver, limit, personalize, secure, and measure advertisements.</p>
    <p>Google and its advertising partners may use advertising cookies to select advertisements based on a visitor’s previous visits to this website or other websites.</p>
    <p>Visitors can manage personalized Google advertising through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
    <p>Information about how Google uses data from websites and apps that use its services is available in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">Google's partner-sites notice</a>.</p>
    <p>Adsterra advertising units are currently disabled. This policy will be updated if another advertising provider is enabled in the future.</p>
    <p>Visitors can access the core guide content without creating an account, making a purchase, subscribing to a newsletter, or clicking an advertisement.</p>

    <h2>Search and browser processing</h2>
    <p>Site search uses a static Pagefind index in the visitor's browser. The query can appear in the page URL so it can be restored on reload. The site does not send that query to an advertising script. Browser extensions, network providers, and the visitor's own browser may handle URLs according to their separate settings.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>There is no contact form, user account, comment system, purchase flow, or newsletter on this site. Selecting the public email link opens the visitor's email software or provider; the resulting message is handled by the sender's provider and the site's configured receiving route, not by a form database on this website.</p>

    <h2>Cloudflare analytics, hosting and security</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled on the production domain to provide aggregate traffic and performance measurement. Cloudflare also delivers and protects the site. It may process limited request and security data such as IP address, browser and device information, requested URL, approximate location, and abuse or threat signals. Cloudflare handles that infrastructure data under its own policies and retention controls.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Links to Steam, Dazed Games announcements, media, videos, community sources, email providers, Google settings, and policy pages open third-party services with their own privacy terms. Following a link is not required to read the main guide text.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This page will be revised when analytics, advertising, consent, contact, or hosting practices materially change. A future consent-management section and footer settings link will be published only after a real Google-certified consent message is live and can reopen its choices.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
